* Number: #534
* Comments: 1
* Linked PRs: #539 (merged)
* Closed by: github.com/honojs/hono/pull/539
When try to set multiple cookies with c.cookie() only the last cookie gets set. Example
export async function Cookies(c: Context) {
    c.cookie("cookie1", "value1")
    c.cookie("cookie2", "value2")
    return c.html('<h1>You should have two cookies!</h1>')
}
This results in only cookie2 being set.
The work around that I am currently using is
export async function Cookies(c: Context) {
    const cookies = {
        cookie1: "value1",
        cookie2: "value2"
    }
    Object.entries(cookies).forEach(cookie => c.res.headers.append('set-cookie', `${cookie.join('=')};`))
    return c.html('<h1>You should have two cookies!</h1>')
}

